{
 "audio": "faucet_take2_cepat115.mp3",
 "speed": 1.15,
 "fps": 30,
 "duration": 70.243,
 "beats": [
  {
   "beat": 1,
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 6.47,
   "frame_start": 0,
   "frame_end": 194,
   "text": "Cut open the pipe behind your sink and water blasts out. Nonstop. It's being pushed at around fifty pounds per square inch."
  },
  {
   "beat": 2,
   "start": 6.609,
   "end": 11.339,
   "frame_start": 198,
   "frame_end": 340,
   "text": "So you jam a metal plug in the hole. It stops. But now you can't get any water at all."
  },
  {
   "beat": 3,
   "start": 11.409,
   "end": 16.974,
   "frame_start": 342,
   "frame_end": 509,
   "text": "So you put the plug on a screw. Turn it one way, the plug lifts. Turn it back, it closes. That's a valve."
  },
  {
   "beat": 4,
   "start": 17.113,
   "end": 21.913,
   "frame_start": 513,
   "frame_end": 657,
   "text": "But it still leaks. Metal on metal never fits perfectly, and water finds every scratch."
  },
  {
   "beat": 5,
   "start": 22.052,
   "end": 27.374,
   "frame_start": 662,
   "frame_end": 821,
   "text": "So you add a soft rubber disc on the end of the plug. It squishes into the gaps and seals. That's a washer."
  },
  {
   "beat": 6,
   "start": 27.548,
   "end": 33.322,
   "frame_start": 826,
   "frame_end": 1000,
   "text": "Now water sneaks up the screw and out around the handle. So you wrap a rubber ring around the stem. That's an O-ring."
  },
  {
   "beat": 7,
   "start": 33.461,
   "end": 40.0,
   "frame_start": 1004,
   "frame_end": 1200,
   "text": "Congrats, you just built a faucet. And here's the problem: every time you shut it off, you crush that rubber and grind it against metal."
  },
  {
   "beat": 8,
   "start": 40.139,
   "end": 48.07,
   "frame_start": 1204,
   "frame_end": 1442,
   "text": "After years of twisting, it goes hard, cracks, and wears a groove. Now there's a gap, and fifty P-S-I pushes water through it, one drop at a time."
  },
  {
   "beat": 9,
   "start": 48.139,
   "end": 52.661,
   "frame_start": 1444,
   "frame_end": 1580,
   "text": "So you crank the handle tighter. That crushes the rubber even more. You just made it worse."
  },
  {
   "beat": 10,
   "start": 52.73,
   "end": 64.0,
   "frame_start": 1582,
   "frame_end": 1920,
   "text": "The fix? Stop squeezing rubber. Use two polished ceramic discs with holes in them. Line the holes up, water flows. Slide them apart, it stops. That's a cartridge, and it's why newer faucets rarely drip."
  },
  {
   "beat": 11,
   "start": 64.07,
   "end": 70.261,
   "frame_start": 1922,
   "frame_end": 2108,
   "text": "One drip a second is more than three thousand gallons a year. But wait, who's pushing all that water into your house in the first place?"
  }
 ],
